-- title:
--   Diamond ⟨ e⟩₀ on the j-finite chart
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ be a subgroup containing every unit that becomes $1$ under the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$, and assume $M/p \neq 0$. Let $hj$ record that the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ`, namely $q^{-1}$ times the integral numerator series of $j$, lies in the intermediate field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the integral form ratios for $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$. Let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a term of the structure `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, which packages integral models at levels `ΓM M H` and `ΓN p M H hpM` over the base ring `R p` together with their properness, flatness, integrality, normality and smoothness data, a curve model over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with its identification of the generic fibre, the chart pins, and the diamond isomorphisms; in particular `𝔛.dia0 e` is the isomorphism attached to $e \in (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ of the level-`ΓN` model, and `.hom` is its forward direction. Let $\sigma$ be an `R p`-algebra automorphism of the $j$-finite chart algebra `chartAlgFin p (ΓN p M H hpM) hj`, the subalgebra of elements of `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (ΓN p M H hpM)` integral over the `R p`-subalgebra generated by the chosen $j$-element, and assume that for every $b$ in that chart algebra the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of $\sigma b$ coincides with the image of the corresponding element of `xHFunctionFieldBar (M/p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM)` under the inverse of the diamond automorphism `diamondAutHBar (M/p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM) e`, where `infSubgroup p M H hpM` is the image of $H$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$. Then the chart morphism `ιFin p (ΓN p M H hpM) hj` followed by `(𝔛.dia0 e).hom` equals $\mathrm{Spec}(\sigma)$ followed by `ιFin p (ΓN p M H hpM) hj`.
--
--   This identifies the diamond isomorphism $\langle e\rangle_0$, which enters the integral model at $p \parallel M$ as data, on the $j$-finite chart of the level-`ΓN` model: it is the spectrum of any chart automorphism realising the inverse diamond automorphism on $q$-expansions. It is the $j$-finite counterpart of the corresponding statement for the $j$-infinite chart, and is used in computing the action of `dia0` on closed points of the special fibre.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XHDRModelAtP_iotaFin_comp_dia0_hom_eq_spec_map_comp_iotaFin.lean

